WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/components/feedback/MaintenanceBanner.tsx — the sticky maintenance / degraded-mode banner. It
  polls /api/v1/system/health (via useSystemHealth) on the standard interval and renders when the
  resolved SystemHealth.mode is "degraded" or "maintenance" (mode "ok" / absent → render nothing).
  Branches reproduced 1:1:
    • mode==='ok' || !data            → render nothing (native friendly empty — never a blank box).
    • maintenance                     → Wrench icon + amber tone; title 'Scheduled maintenance';
                                        body = maintenance_message.trim() || 'Maintenance is in progress.
                                        Live data may be paused.'
    • degraded                        → AlertTriangle icon + sky tone; title 'Service is degraded';
                                        body = maintenance_message.trim() || 'Some features may be slow or
                                        unavailable while we work on it.'
    • live countdown to maintenance_until (1 Hz tick): remaining>1s → 'Ends in {{time}}'
                                        (formatRemaining = "Hh MMm" / "Mm SSs" / "Ss"); >-1s → 'Ending now';
                                        else → 'Window has ended; refresh to confirm.'
    • per-snapshot dismissal keyed on fingerprint(mode,message,until,updatedAt)
                                        ("u:${updatedAt}" if updatedAt else "s:${mode}|${message}|${until}"),
                                        persisted to sessionStorage; reset when the snapshot fingerprint
                                        changes so a freshly-pushed banner re-surfaces. Dismiss control:
                                        aria-label t('common.dismiss','Dismiss').
  Data sources (hooks): useSystemHealth (→ P1/S8 source seam over /system/health), useTranslation
  (→ P1/S10 facade). useAdmin is the hook module that exports useSystemHealth.

